  "description": "Logins to the Discovery Environment, from public.logins in the DE database. A row is written by the apps service when terrain handles GET /secured/bootstrap, keyed on the Keycloak SSO session, so a row is roughly one login rather than one request. All times are the DE database server's local time (America/Phoenix): logins.login_time is a timestamp without time zone, so it carries no offset and is read literally. The dashboard timezone is pinned to UTC so those values are displayed and bucketed exactly as stored -- a daily bucket is a database calendar day. Do not switch the dashboard to browser time; it would shift every bucket boundary. Stats and the by-affiliation panels split users into University of Arizona and other users by joining grafana.ua_users, a view over the user portal database; see the grafana wiki page.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "de-postgres"
      },
      "description": "Total logins over the selected time range, and how many were by University of Arizona and other users. A user counts as University of Arizona if they have a verified email address in the user portal at arizona.edu or one of its subdomains (grafana.ua_users in the DE database).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "fixedColor": "text",
            "mode": "fixed"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
